deCone(CentralArrangement,RingElement) -- produce an affine arrangement from a central one
******************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note deCone: deCone_lpCentralArrangement_cmRingElement_rp,
  * Usage: 
        deCone(A, x)
        deCone(A, i)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note central hyperplane arrangement: CentralArrangement,, 
      * x, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a hyperplane of
        $A$ or the index of a hyperplane of $A$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hyperplane arrangement: Arrangement,, the decone of $A$ over
        $x$

Description
===========

The decone of a *note central arrangement: CentralArrangement, $A$ at a
hyperplane $H=H_i$ or $H=\ker x$ is the affine arrangement obtained from $A$ by
first deleting the hyperplane $H$ then intersecting the remaining hyperplanes
with the (affine) hyperplane $\{x=1\}$. In particular, if $R$ is the *note
coordinate ring: ring_lpArrangement_rp, of $A$, then the coordinate ring of its
decone over $x$ is $R/(x-1)$.

The decone of a *note central arrangement: CentralArrangement, at $H$ can also
be constructed by first projectivizing $A$, then removing the image of $H$, and
identifying the complement of $H$ with affine space.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = arrangement "X3"                   |
|                                            |
|o1 = {x , x , x , x  + x , x  + x , x  + x }|
|       1   2   3   1    2   1    3   2    3 |
|                                            |
|o1 : Hyperplane Arrangement                 |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : dA = deCone(A,2)                       |
|                                            |
|o2 = {x , x , x  + x , x  + 1, x  + 1}      |
|       1   2   1    2   1       2           |
|                                            |
|o2 : Hyperplane Arrangement                 |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : factor poincare A                      |
|                                            |
|                        2                   |
|o3 = (1 + T)(1 + 5T + 7T )                  |
|                                            |
|o3 : Expression of class Product            |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : poincare dA                            |
|                                            |
|                2                           |
|o4 = 1 + 5T + 7T                            |
|                                            |
|o4 : ZZ[T]                                  |
+--------------------------------------------+

The coordinate ring of $dA$ is $\mathbb{Q}[x_1,x_2,x_3]/(x_3-1)$.

+-----------------+
|i5 : ring dA     |
|                 |
|     QQ[x ..x ]  |
|         1   3   |
|o5 = ----------  |
|       x  - 1    |
|        3        |
|                 |
|o5 : QuotientRing|
+-----------------+

Use *note prune: prune_lpArrangement_rp, to get something whose coordinate ring
is a polynomial ring.

+--------------------------------------+
|i6 : dA' = prune dA                   |
|                                      |
|o6 = {x , x , x  + x , x  + 1, x  + 1}|
|       1   2   1    2   1       2     |
|                                      |
|o6 : Hyperplane Arrangement           |
+--------------------------------------+
|i7 : ring dA'                         |
|                                      |
|o7 = QQ[x ..x ]                       |
|         1   2                        |
|                                      |
|o7 : PolynomialRing                   |
+--------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note cone(Arrangement,RingElement): cone_lpArrangement_cmRingElement_rp,
    -- creates an associated central hyperplane arrangement

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note deCone(CentralArrangement,RingElement):
    deCone_lpCentralArrangement_cmRingElement_rp, -- produce an affine
    arrangement from a central one
  * "deCone(CentralArrangement,ZZ)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

