euler(CentralArrangement) -- compute the Euler characteristic of the projective complement
******************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note euler: (Macaulay2Doc)euler,
  * Usage: 
        euler A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note central hyperplane arrangement: CentralArrangement,, or a
        *note Flat: Flat,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, equal to the Euler characteristic

Description
===========

For any topological space, the Euler characteristic is the alternating sum of
its Betti numbers (a.k.a. the ranks of its homology groups).  For a central
hyperplane arrangement, the associated topological space is the
projectivization of its complement.

The Euler characteristic for the hyperplane arrangements defined by root
systems are described by simple formulas.

+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A2 = typeA 2                                                 |
|                                                                  |
|o1 = {x  - x , x  - x , x  - x }                                  |
|       1    2   1    3   2    3                                   |
|                                                                  |
|o1 : Hyperplane Arrangement                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : euler A2                                                     |
|                                                                  |
|o2 = -1                                                           |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : assert all(5, n -> euler typeA (n+1) === (-1)^(n) * n!)      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : B2 = typeB 2                                                 |
|                                                                  |
|o4 = {x , x  - x , x  + x , x }                                   |
|       1   1    2   1    2   2                                    |
|                                                                  |
|o4 : Hyperplane Arrangement                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : euler B2                                                     |
|                                                                  |
|o5 = -2                                                           |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert all(4, n -> euler typeB (n+1) === (-1)^(n) * 2^n * n!)|
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

Given a flat, this method computes the Euler characteristic of the
subarrangement indexed by the flat.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : A4 = typeA 4                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = {x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x ,|
|       1    2   1    3   1    4   1    5   2    3   2    4   2    5   3    4 |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : Hyperplane Arrangement                                                  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x  - x , x  - x }                                                            |
| 3    5   4    5                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : F = flat(A4, {0,7})                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = {0, 7}                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o8 : Flat of {x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , |
|               1    2   1    3   1    4   1    5   2    3   2    4   2    5  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x  - x , x  - x , x  - x }                                                   |
| 3    4   3    5   4    5                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : euler F                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = 0                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert(euler A4_F === euler F)                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : euler flat(A4, {2,3,9})                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o11 = -1                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : euler flat(A4, {0,1,2,4,5,7})                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o12 = 2                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : euler flat(A4, {2,4,6,8})                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o13 = 0                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The Euler characteristic of the empty arrangement is just the Euler
characteristic of the ambient projective space.  For instance, the Euler
characteristic of the complex projective plane is $3$.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : assert (euler arrangement({}, ring A2) === 3)|
+---------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note typeA: typeA_lpZZ_cmRing_rp, -- make the hyperplane arrangement
    defined by a type $A_n$ root system
  * *note typeB: typeB_lpZZ_cmRing_rp, -- make the hyperplane arrangement
    defined by a type $B_n$ root system
  * *note subArrangement: subArrangement_lpArrangement_cmFlat_rp, -- create the
    hyperplane arrangement containing a flat
  * *note flat: flat_lpArrangement_cmList_rp, -- make a flat from a list of
    indices

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note euler(CentralArrangement): euler_lpCentralArrangement_rp, -- compute
    the Euler characteristic of the projective complement
  * "euler(Flat)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

