genericArrangement(ZZ,ZZ,Ring) -- realize the uniform matroid using points on the monomial curve
************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note genericArrangement: genericArrangement_lpZZ_cmZZ_cmRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        genericArrangement(r,n,K)
        genericArrangement(r,n)
  * Inputs:
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the rank of the arrangement
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of hyperplanes
      * K, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a coefficient ring: $\QQ$ by
        default
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hyperplane arrangement: Arrangement,, the arrangement with
        linear forms normal to $(1,j,j^2,\cdots,j^{r-1})$, for $1\leq j\leq n$.

Description
===========

By definition, a generic arrangement is a realization of a uniform matroid
$U_{r,n}$, which is characterized by the property that all subsets of the
ground set of size at most $r$ are independent. Points on the monomial curve
have this property.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : poincare genericArrangement(3,5,QQ)|
|                                        |
|                 2     3                |
|o1 = 1 + 5T + 10T  + 6T                 |
|                                        |
|o1 : ZZ[T]                              |
+----------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note randomArrangement: randomArrangement_lpZZ_cmPolynomialRing_cmZZ_rp,
    -- generate an arrangement at random

