graphic(List,List,PolynomialRing) -- make a graphic arrangement
***************************************************************

  * Function: *note graphic: graphic_lpList_cmList_cmPolynomialRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        graphic(E, V, R)
        graphic(E, R)
        graphic(E, V)
        graphic E
  * Inputs:
      * E, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the edges of a graph expressed as
        a list of pairs of vertices as specified in $V$
      * V, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the vertices of a graph expressed
        as a list of elements
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, an optional
        coordinate ring for the arrangement or a *note ring:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Ring, to be interpreted as a coefficient ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hyperplane arrangement: Arrangement,, associated to the given
        graph

Description
===========

A graph $G$ is specified by a list $V$ of vertices and a list $E$ of pairs of
vertices.  When $V$ is not specified, it is assumed to be the list $1, 2,
\ldots, n$, where $n$ is the largest integer appearing as a vertex of $E$. The
graphic arrangement $A(G)$ of $G$ is the subarrangement of the *note type
$A_{n-1}$ arrangement: typeA_lpZZ_cmRing_rp, with hyperplanes $x_i-x_j$ for
each edge $\{i,j\}$ of the graph $G$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = {{1,2},{2,3},{3,4},{4,1}}; -- a four-cycle              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : AG = graphic G                                              |
|                                                                 |
|o2 = {- x  + x , - x  + x , - x  + x , x  - x }                  |
|         1    2     2    3     3    4   1    4                   |
|                                                                 |
|o2 : Hyperplane Arrangement                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : rank AG -- the number of vertices minus number of components|
|                                                                 |
|o3 = 3                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : ring AG                                                     |
|                                                                 |
|o4 = QQ[x ..x ]                                                  |
|         1   4                                                   |
|                                                                 |
|o4 : PolynomialRing                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

One can also specify the ambient ring.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : AG' = graphic(G,QQ[x,y,z,w]) -- four variables because there are 4      |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {- x + y, - y + z, - z + w, x - w}                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : Hyperplane Arrangement                                                  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|vertices                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : ring AG'                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = QQ[x..z, w]                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Occasionally, one might want to give labels to the vertices. These labels can
be anything!

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : V = {"a", "b", "c", "d"};                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : E = {{"a","b"}, {"b", "c"}, {"c","d"}, {"d","a"}};|
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : graphic(E, V)                                     |
|                                                       |
|o9 = {- x  + x , - x  + x , - x  + x , x  - x }        |
|         1    2     2    3     3    4   1    4         |
|                                                       |
|o9 : Hyperplane Arrangement                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

The vertices can also be the variables of a polynomial ring.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d];                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : arr = graphic({{a,b},{b,c},{c,d},{d,a}}, gens R, R)|
|                                                         |
|o11 = {- a + b, - b + c, - c + d, a - d}                 |
|                                                         |
|o11 : Hyperplane Arrangement                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : ring arr === R                                     |
|                                                         |
|o12 = true                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

Loops and parallel edges are allowed.

+-----------------------------+
|i13 : graphic({{1,2}, {1,2}})|
|                             |
|o13 = {- x  + x , - x  + x } |
|          1    2     1    2  |
|                             |
|o13 : Hyperplane Arrangement |
+-----------------------------+
|i14 : graphic({{1,1}, {1,2}})|
|                             |
|o14 = {0, - x  + x }         |
|             1    2          |
|                             |
|o14 : Hyperplane Arrangement |
+-----------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note arrangement(List): arrangement_lpList_cmRing_rp, -- make a hyperplane
    arrangement
  * *note typeA: typeA_lpZZ_cmRing_rp, -- make the hyperplane arrangement
    defined by a type $A_n$ root system
  * *note rank(CentralArrangement): rank_lpCentralArrangement_rp, -- compute
    the rank of a central hyperplane arrangement

