isDecomposable(CentralArrangement,Ring) -- whether a hyperplane arrangement decomposable in the sense of Papadima-Suciu
***********************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isDecomposable:
    isDecomposable_lpCentralArrangement_cmRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        isDecomposable(A, R)
        isDecomposable A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note central hyperplane arrangement: CentralArrangement,, 
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, an optional coefficient ring used
        as the coefficient field for the holonomy Lie algebra.  If unspecified,
        R=QQ
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is *note true:
        (Macaulay2Doc)true, if the hyperplane arrangement decomposes in the
        sense of Papadima and Suciu over the given coefficient field

Description
===========

Following Definition 2.3 in Stefan Papadima and Alexander I. Suciu's paper
"When does the associated graded Lie algebra of an arrangement group
decompose?", Commentarii Mathematici Helvetici (2006) 859-875,
arXiv:math/0309324 (see https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0309324 ), a hyperplane
arrangement is decomposable if the derived subalgebra of its holonomy Lie
algebra is a direct sum of the derived subalgebras of free Lie algebras,
indexed by the rank-2 *note flats: Flat, of the arrangement.

As described in the introduction of Papadima-Suciu, the X3 arrangement is
decomposable.  The hyperplane arrangement defined by a type $A_3$ root system
is not decomposable.  The authors show that a *note graphic arrangement:
graphic_lpList_cmList_cmPolynomialRing_rp, is decomposable over ${\mathbb Q}$
if and only if it is decomposable over any other field.  In general, it is not
known if there exist arrangements for which property of being decomposable
depends on the choice of field.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X3 = arrangement "X3"                  |
|                                            |
|o1 = {x , x , x , x  + x , x  + x , x  + x }|
|       1   2   3   1    2   1    3   2    3 |
|                                            |
|o1 : Hyperplane Arrangement                 |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : assert isDecomposable X3               |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : assert isDecomposable(X3, ZZ/5)        |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert not isDecomposable typeA 3      |
+--------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Flat: Flat, -- intersection of hyperplanes
  * *note orlikSolomon: orlikSolomon_lpArrangement_cmPolynomialRing_rp, --
    compute the defining ideal for the Orlik-Solomon algebra

Ways to use this method:
========================

