*************************************************************************

  * Function: *note meet: meet_lpFlat_cmFlat_rp,
  * Usage: 
        meet(F, G)
        F ^ G
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note flat in an hyperplane arrangement: Flat,, 
      * G, a *note flat in an hyperplane arrangement: Flat,, in the same
        arrangement as $F$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note flat in an hyperplane arrangement: Flat,, having the greatest
        codimension among those contained in both $F$ and $G$

Description
===========

In the geometric lattice of flats, the meet (also known as the infimum or
greatest lower bound) is the intersection of the flats. Equivalently,
identifying flats with subspaces, this operation is the Minkowski sum of the
subspaces.

The meet operation is commutative, associative, and idempotent.

