prune(Arrangement) -- makes a new hyperplane arrangement in a polynomial ring
*****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note prune: (Macaulay2Doc)prune,
  * Usage: 
        prune A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note hyperplane arrangement: Arrangement,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Exclude: (Macaulay2Doc)minimalPresentation_lpRing_rp, => ...,
        default value {}, this optional input is ignored by this function
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hyperplane arrangement: Arrangement,, an isomorphic to the
        input but defined over a polynomial ring

Description
===========

A hyperplane arrangement may sensibly be defined over a quotient of a *note
polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing, by a linear ideal. However,
sometimes this is inconvenient.  This method creates an isomorphic hyperplane
arrangement in a polynomial ring.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = typeA 3                                                 |
|                                                                 |
|o1 = {x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x }      |
|       1    2   1    3   1    4   2    3   2    4   3    4       |
|                                                                 |
|o1 : Hyperplane Arrangement                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A'' = restriction(A,0) -- restrict A to its first hyperplane|
|                                                                 |
|o2 = {x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x }               |
|       2    3   2    4   2    3   2    4   3    4                |
|                                                                 |
|o2 : Hyperplane Arrangement                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : ring A''                                                    |
|                                                                 |
|      QQ[x ..x ]                                                 |
|          1   4                                                  |
|o3 = ------------                                                |
|     (x  - x , 0)                                                |
|       1    2                                                    |
|                                                                 |
|o3 : QuotientRing                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : B = prune A''                                               |
|                                                                 |
|o4 = {x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x , x  - x }               |
|       2    3   2    4   2    3   2    4   3    4                |
|                                                                 |
|o4 : Hyperplane Arrangement                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : ring B                                                      |
|                                                                 |
|o5 = QQ[x ..x ]                                                  |
|         2   4                                                   |
|                                                                 |
|o5 : PolynomialRing                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

