vee(Flat,Flat) -- compute the vee operation in the intersection lattice
***********************************************************************

  * Function: *note vee: vee_lpFlat_cmFlat_rp,
  * Usage: 
        vee(F, G)
        F | G
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note flat in an hyperplane arrangement: Flat,, 
      * G, a *note flat in an hyperplane arrangement: Flat,, in the same
        arrangement as $F$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note flat in an hyperplane arrangement: Flat,, having the least
        codimension among those contained in both $F$ and $G$

Description
===========

In the geometric lattice of flats, the vee (also known as the supremum or least
upper bound) is the join operation. Equivalently, identifying flats with
subspaces, this operation is the closure of the union.

The vee operation is commutative, associative, and idempotent.

